   "page": 5,
   "fixture": true,
   "description": "A pulse generator with 50 Ω source resistance pushes a forward current pulse through 1 kΩ into the anode of the diode under test, whose cathode is grounded. The anode is watched through 450 Ω by a 50 Ω oscilloscope input, and the overshoot of the forward voltage at turn-on is VFR. The pulse rises in 20 ns, lasts at least 100 ns and repeats at a duty cycle of at most 0.005.",
